```js
function findDuplicates(ids) {
  const seen = new Set()
  const dupes = new Set()
  for (const id of ids) {
    if (seen.has(id)) dupes.add(id)
    else seen.add(id)
  }
  return [...dupes]
}
// findDuplicates([101, 205, 101, 330, 205]) -> [101, 205]
// findDuplicates([]) -> []
```
Tiempo O(n), memoria O(n). Narración clave: *My first idea is two nested loops, O(n²). I can do better by remembering what I've seen in a Set.*

```js
function pairForBudget(prices, budget) {
  const seen = new Map() // precio -> índice
  for (let i = 0; i < prices.length; i++) {
    const need = budget - prices[i]
    if (seen.has(need)) return [seen.get(need), i]
    seen.set(prices[i], i)
  }
  return null
}
```
O(n) tiempo y memoria. Buscar antes de guardar evita usar el mismo producto dos veces.
